ain","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"If a function has a trailing comma in the argument list, black does not remove it.\r\n\r\nStart from:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef one(\r\n    a,\r\n):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\ndef two(\r\n    a,\r\n    b,\r\n):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\nRun black over that file, and you get:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef one(a,):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef two(\r\n    a, b,\r\n):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would expect something more like:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef one(a):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef two(a, b):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Environment:**\r\n\r\n- Version: I can reproduce this in release and master builds; 19.10b0 and 19.10b1.dev16+g1ab87a3\r\n- OS and Python version: macOS, Python 3.7.5\r\n\r\n**Does this bug also happen on master?** Yes.\r\n\r\n**Additional context** \r\n\r\nPossibly related issues:\r\n\r\n- #880 Trailing comma for function with one arg, which is where I took the minimal example from. Unlike that issue, this seems to affect functions with more than one argument.\r\n- #1136 tracks the bug where it's not collapsing the argument list of `two(a, b)` into a single line.\r\n\r\nI had a look for duplicates in the trailing-comma label, couldn't find any.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/1228/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/1228/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]